// EN translation FIRST PASS. Literary editorial approval outstanding.
const OUTCOMES_EN_E361_E430 = Object.freeze({"E361.1":{"s":"Vern agrees to give G-17 a well-deserved day off, and for the first time the builders discuss taking a break for themselves. They pay the party gold for mediation.","f":"Vern refuses to change the schedule because of the chalk writing. G-17 remains motionless, and construction does not progress."},"E361.2":{"s":"You share supplies with workers forced to wait for the block to rise. Vern pays in gold for help on a day of unplanned downtime."},"E361.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} checks the G-17 hinges and confirms that there is no breakdown: the golem itself stopped working. Vern pays gold for a clear answer.","f":"When checked, a massive block slides off the support and seriously injures {{affectedHeroName}}. The reason for the golem stopping was never determined.","v":{"nf":"The block is torn from its support, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. G-17 still refuses to work."}},"E361.4":{"s":"You leave G-17 and Vern to discuss twenty-three years of working seven days a week. Builders are already adapting this right to their own schedule."},"E362.1":{"s":"You force K-4 to give out coins for the wrong product. Nara thanks gold for stopping the trade in spoons.","f":"K-4 opens the drawer again and gives out the spoon instead of returning it. The line of customers is only getting longer."},"E362.2":{"s":"You buy supplies directly from Nara, bypassing the stubborn machine. K-4, meanwhile, offers a wooden spoon to another customer."},"E362.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} detects a looped spoon dispensing command in the control circuit. Nara pays gold for the cause found.","f":"The copper mechanism suddenly squeezes the working hand, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded.","v":{"nf":"The machine gun slams the service compartment, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. The spoons keep falling out."}},"E362.4":{"s":"You don't risk buying bread from a machine with only one answer. People in the square are already arguing about how many spoons count as one sack of flour."},"E363.1":{"s":"You cross the barrier without waiting for M-8 permission and go through the gate. The changing of the guard looks at you with envy.","f":"The guard declares the attempt to pass as a violation of the order and raises the combat constructs. The battle begins."},"E363.2":{"s":"You buy supplies from the caravaners and settle down to wait while Sena deals with the bronze guard. The password is heard from behind the gate, which is again recognized as correct."},"E363.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} detects two mutually exclusive orders: the password is correct, but the old ban has not been cancelled. Sena corrects the order and thanks him with gold.","f":"{{heroName}} finds the seals of both orders authentic, but neither has seniority. M-8 is still prohibited."},"E363.4":{"s":"You spend supplies going around the gate and leave Sen to explain himself to the guard. M-8 once again confirms that the password is correct."},"E364.1":{"s":"You remain in the square and notice how the missed minute leaves a gold item of an unknown owner at the watch. The find replenishes the treasury.","f":"Exactly before noon, armed strangers appear on the square, as if dropped out of a vanished moment. A skirmish begins."},"E364.2":{"s":"You buy supplies from Ir and leave before twelve. The watchmaker promises not to blink this time when the hands jump."},"E364.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} recognizes a short gap in the rune dial and finds the gold hidden underneath. Ir thanks for the solution.","f":"When the hands miss a minute, {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded by a sudden blow from the clockwork.","v":{"nf":"The clock ends the observation with a dangerous jump, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. The missing minute remains a mystery."}},"E364.4":{"s":"You leave Ir to watch the minute, which his watch refuses to show. The square is already preparing a place for tomorrow's trail."},"E365.1":{"s":"Doon sits down opposite L-3 and hears a familiar story about his mother, not daring to interrupt. For the opportunity to talk, Master Kira gives the party gold.","f":"Doon can't stand it when the construct says the pet name of his childhood and ends the conversation. There is no explanation."},"E365.2":{"s":"You leave supplies for Kira for new memory tests. The master thanks him with gold, and L-3 continues to tell someone else’s childhood."},"E365.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} discovers in the construct’s memory a trace of an old recording that matches Dun’s story. Kira thanks the gold for the lead.","f":"The Hidden Memory Seal knocks back the explorer and {{affectedHeroName}} is severely injured.","v":{"nf":"The memory seal interrupts the exploration, but no eligible combatants are gravely wounded. Dun and L-3 remain unanswered."}},"E365.4":{"s":"You don't decide for Doon and L-3 who owns one memory of Cell. They keep talking about a house that is long gone."},"E366.1":{"s":"You acknowledge P-1's right to decide for himself whether to continue serving. Tesa pays in gold for honest mediation, although she has not yet begun dismantling.","f":"Tesa refuses to accept the machine's request as a final decision. R-1 can only wait for the conversation, not the tools."},"E366.2":{"s":"R-1 agrees to first stop working and live without assignments. The students give the party supplies for the opportunity to think about their choices without rushing.","f":"R-1 considers the pause to be another imposed task and refuses your offer. The dispute remains open."},"E366.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} checks R-1's memory and mechanisms, finding no error that would explain the request. Tesa pays in gold for verification.","f":"When the working compartment is opened, the protection is triggered, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded.","v":{"nf":"The hull protection disrupts the inspection, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. The reason for the request cannot be confirmed."}},"E366.4":{"s":"You don't make a decision instead of an intelligent machine and walk away. R-1 stays with Tesa so that they can negotiate without strangers."},"E367.1":{"s":"You offer the crow a polished button, and he gives you some stolen coins for it. Gold replenishes the treasury.","f":"The bird looks at your shiny junk, then decisively turns away to someone else's helmet. The deal did not go through."},"E367.2":{"s":"You return some of the coins stolen by the bird to Emma, and the merchant shares the food for the road. Raven is already evaluating her new clasp.","f":"Emma cannot prove which coin was missing from her cart and refuses to exchange it. The party does not receive supplies."},"E367.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} exchanges an unnecessary iron buckle for a crow's supply of gold, preserving the party's valuables.","f":"Raven grabs the real gold clasp from the belt and takes it away before {{heroName}} can intervene. The treasury is losing gold."},"E367.4":{"s":"You leave the raven to rule the market for shiny things. Emma counts the coins while one carter polishes a spoon with his sleeve."},"E368.1":{"s":"You wait until a forgotten boat full of gold floats down the river and the deer finally retreats from the bridge. The find goes to the party.","f":"Armed strangers appear under the bridge, coming downstream after an unknown object. A skirmish begins."},"E368.2":{"s":"You use up your supplies to cross the ford without disturbing the deer. He still looks down at the river."},"E368.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} explores the current and finds gold with surviving supplies near the old piles. The deer turns its head towards the shore for the first time.","f":"On the washed-out edge of the shore, {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded when the ground collapses under his feet.","v":{"nf":"The coast crumbles under reconnaissance, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. The reason for waiting for the deer cannot be found out."}},"E368.4":{"s":"You don't disturb the deer waiting on the narrow bridge. He takes another step back when a log floats beneath him."},"E369.1":{"s":"You distract the bear and return the bell to the monks without new cracks. The bell ringer Pir thanks in gold for the saved shrine.","f":"The bear clutches the bell in its paws and suddenly runs into {{affectedHeroName}}, causing severe injury.","v":{"nf":"The bear fights off an attempt to take the toy, but none of the eligible combatants are gravely wounded. The bell remains in the forest."}},"E369.2":{"s":"You leave supplies for the monks to continue the chase. The feast gives thanks in gold as the bell rings again far away among the trees."},"E369.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} leads the bear to an open slope, where the monks manage to exchange the bell for a large metal cauldron. The feast pays in gold.","f":"In a narrow passage, the bear suddenly rushes to the side, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded.","v":{"nf":"The bear breaks the enclosure, but none of the eligible combatants are gravely wounded. The ringing continues to fade."}},"E369.4":{"s":"You leave the monks to pursue the ringing, which can already be heard two miles away. The forest responds to each bearish step with a new sound of the bell."},"E370.1":{"s":"You help Lem lead the geese from the parade ground to a distant meadow, and the soldiers return to the line. In gratitude, they give out supplies.","f":"The geese refuse to leave the sergeant and line up behind him even more tightly. It is impossible to take them away from the camp."},"E370.2":{"s":"You buy supplies from the soldiers while Lem tries to take the whistle from the goose. The bird responds with a particularly loud hiss."},"E370.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} finds out that the geese do not obey commands, but the whistle that the leader stole. Lem thanks in gold for the solution.","f":"{{heroName}} tries all the drill commands, but the geese only perform those they like. The sergeant is left without a decision."},"E370.4":{"s":"You leave Lem in command of the pack that appointed him. One goose strides ahead with a stolen whistle."},"E371.1":{"s":"You move the old lion aside without raising a weapon at him. Relatives can finally see the hunter off and thank him with gold.","f":"The lion takes the approach as a threat to the deceased and comes out to meet him with his claws drawn. A skirmish begins."},"E371.2":{"s":"You leave supplies for the family for the long wait. The hunter's mother thanks him with gold while the lion continues to lie at the grave."},"E371.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} suggests saying goodbye where the lion lies, without driving him away from the body. The family pays in gold for the opportunity to bury their own.","f":"The lion jerks into the path of the funeral rite, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded.","v":{"nf":"The beast stops the ritual, but none of the eligible combatants are gravely wounded. The funeral has to be postponed."}},"E371.4":{"s":"You don't stop the old lion from saying goodbye to the hunter. The mother stops her son as he reaches for the weapon again."},"E372.1":{"s":"You follow the trail of the owner and find a golden purse left at an old ford. The dogs continue to guard the empty cart.","f":"The trail leads to an ambush by armed men who knew about the missing driver. The battle begins."},"E372.2":{"s":"You leave some of the food for the dogs near the empty bowls. None of the six leaves the cart until the food is eaten."},"E372.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} follows the first few miles of the trail and finds the missing driver's gold box in a hiding place. The party takes her without touching the dogs.","f":"On the pursuit path, {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded by a hidden trap.","v":{"nf":"The trail leads to a dangerous place, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. The owner cannot be found."}},"E372.4":{"s":"You leave the cart and six faithful guards on the road. The owner's glove remains lying on the folded blanket."},"E373.1":{"s":"You explain to Nima that yesterday was not because of the watch repair. The watchmaker thanks in gold for the dropped claim.","f":"Nima demands a receipt for returning yesterday and does not recognize the word about the calendar. The watchmaker winds the watch again."},"E373.2":{"s":"You buy supplies from the watchmaker and leave while Nima fills out an imaginary plaintive book of time."},"E373.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} shows the fairy that what was paid for was repairing the clock, not stopping the calendar. The watchmaker pays in gold for a clear decision.","f":"{{heroName}} does not find a formulation that Nima is ready to accept: she still demands the unlived day. The dispute continues."},"E373.4":{"s":"You do not promise Nima to return yesterday and continue on your way. Behind you you can hear the fairy demanding a plaintive book for tomorrow."},"E374.1":{"s":"Clem agrees to leave the old boot to the ants along with the buckle. Anisa thanks the party with supplies for saving the temple.","f":"Clem does not want to give the silver buckle to the ant priesthood and reaches for the boot. It is not possible to reach an agreement."},"E374.2":{"s":"You pay Clem for the rights to the buckle, but leave the miniature temple untouched. The ants continue to guard their sanctuary."},"E374.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} recognizes in ant rituals the custom of consecrating a found shelter. Anisa thanks gold for the explanation.","f":"{{heroName}} cannot understand the movements of the tiny priests. The ants continue to protect the buckle."},"E374.4":{"s":"You leave the new shrine to its small parishioners. Clem thoughtfully assesses how many of his old shoes are still suitable for temples."},"E375.1":{"s":"You turn away from the butterfly and pretend to take a different path while she leads the party to the food cache. Supplies are being replenished.","f":"The butterfly notices that the pursuit is too obvious and returns to the original stone. The search for a detour takes up supplies."},"E375.2":{"s":"You pay Al for the regular route, which doesn't involve tricking the butterfly. The conductor takes up the map with noticeable relief."},"E375.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} chooses a path to the side, and the butterfly voluntarily shows a short passage to food supplies. The party receives supplies.","f":"On a diversionary route, {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded by a hidden obstacle.","v":{"nf":"The false route leads into a dangerous passage, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. The butterfly returns to the stone."}},"E375.4":{"s":"You choose the path without cunning and leave Al to argue with the behavior of the butterfly. She sits on a stone as if she understands everything."},"E376.1":{"s":"You carefully replant the plucked flower back into the protected grove. The ladybug guard frees the caravan, and Ram thanks him with supplies.","f":"The flower does not take root in the same place, and the ladybug does not remove the detention. The caravan remains near the grove."},"E376.2":{"s":"You share provisions with drivers stuck on the road. Merchant Ram thanks in gold for his help during the arrest."},"E376.3":{"s":"{{heroName}}, through a translator, suggests replanting the flower and protecting it until it takes root. Ladybug agrees, and Ram gives out the gold.","f":"{{heroName}} cannot convince the guard that a fine will replace the return of the flower. The road remains closed."},"E376.4":{"s":"You bypass the detained caravan and do not get into an argument about a plucked flower. The fairy translator continues to patiently move her antennae instead of a guard."},"E377.1":{"s":"Pieck agrees to leave the helmet before the tournament when Dorn promises her new housing. The knight thanks in gold for the freed protection.","f":"The fairy shows the lease agreement before the first thunderstorm and does not intend to move when the sky is clear. Dorn is left without a helmet."},"E377.2":{"s":"You pay Peak for relocation, and the fairy brings out a tiny bed with a curtain from the helmet. Dorn checks to see if she forgot her socks."},"E377.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} adapts an empty lamp with safe ventilation for Peak, and the fairy voluntarily releases the helmet. Dorn thanks with gold.","f":"{{heroName}} does not find a dwelling that Peak would consider as comfortable as a knight's helmet. The move is postponed."},"E377.4":{"s":"You wish Dorn good weather before the tournament. The fairy assures that the first thunderstorm will come someday anyway."},"E378.1":{"s":"You manage to buy supplies before the last strike of the bell and take them out of the disappearing market.","f":"The market disappears when the seller is still counting the change, and the commission for the unfinished transaction remains with you. The treasury loses additional gold."},"E378.2":{"s":"You resell ready-made parcels to hurrying buyers and receive gold before the end of the minute.","f":"Buyers rush past your offers, and the market disappears before anyone makes a deal."},"E378.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} marks the necessary shops in advance, and the party gets to them in a few moments. Supplies purchased before the market disappeared.","f":"{{heroName}} makes a mistake with the order of the tents, and some of the supplies are lost in the last-second crush."},"E378.4":{"s":"You watch how in one minute the whole square disappears along with the market. The man with the list on his sleeve is still looking at his empty hands."},"E379.1":{"s":"You buy a map from Zhik and find a real gold cache under the floorboards. Mopa immediately demands to see what else her husband has marked as secret.","f":"The hiding place under the floorboard turns out to be empty, although the map is quite accurate. Coins paid for the plan are not refundable."},"E379.2":{"s":"You buy supplies from Mopa instead of a family house map. She asks not to tell Zhik that the pantry also has a price."},"E379.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} finds a useful cache mark on the plan, not intended for strangers. Zhik gives out gold to avoid a family scandal.","f":"{{heroName}} detects only renamed home rooms. There is no safe haven on the map."},"E379.4":{"s":"You leave Zhik and Mopa to argue about the hiding place under the floorboard. A map of your own home suddenly becomes family evidence."},"E380.1":{"s":"You show the farmers a wooden paw and force Grix to return the insurance premiums. The party receives gold for exposure.","f":"Grix calls the wooden paw proof of a particularly cunning dragon and calls for armed assistants. A skirmish begins."},"E380.2":{"s":"You buy supplies from farmers while they find out the purpose of the wooden paw from the insurer."},"E380.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} finds in the contract a clause about a real dragon footprint and presents a wooden fake. Grix returns the gold.","f":"{{heroName}} cannot prove that Grix himself forged the trail, and the insurer charges a fee for legal analysis. The treasury is losing gold."},"E380.4":{"s":"You refuse to buy insurance against a dragon that no one has seen. Grix is ​​already convincing farmers that real monsters also have wooden paws."},"E381.1":{"s":"Bulk pours you a “royal dinner” from a common cauldron; camping bowls are replenished with supplies. It’s hard to tell the difference with “traveler’s soup.”"},"E381.2":{"s":"You place four identical plates in front of Bulk, and he reluctantly returns the gold difference for the imaginary variety.","f":"The chef declares the difference to be purely emotional, and no one can prove otherwise. No discount."},"E381.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} discovers a large supply of food behind the kitchen, which Bulk never used. For silence about the warehouse, the cook gives out supplies.","f":"{{heroName}} hits a loose shelf, and some of the party's supplies are spoiled along with the contents of the kitchen."},"E381.4":{"s":"You leave the restaurant with twenty-three names for one stew. Bulk is already adding number twenty-four to the menu."},"E382.1":{"s":"The inspector sees the rat confidently walking around the hole and allows Pook to continue on his way. The driver pays in gold for the saved trip.","f":"The inspector demands the driver's signature, and the rat leaves a mark of teeth on the paper. Still no permission."},"E382.2":{"s":"You buy supplies from Puk directly from the back. The rat patiently holds the reins while he searches for the bags."},"E382.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} checks the harness and notices that the rat reacts to turns before the owner. The inspector thanks him with gold for the test.","f":"{{heroName}} cannot convince the inspector to admit driving without a signature. The cart remains by the side of the road."},"E382.4":{"s":"You are not involved in issuing rights to rats. Puk falls asleep again, and his little driver patiently waits for permission."},"E383.1":{"s":"You return the bills to Zib, and the banker immediately checks the balance on all accounts. He pays for saved operations in gold.","f":"The boy does not want to part with the beads, and Zib refuses to count without them. Negotiations reach a dead end."},"E383.2":{"s":"Zeeb agrees to pay a large reward and is relieved to receive his bills. Gold goes to the treasury.","f":"The banker declares the proposed amount impossible, and for the discussion collects gold at the bank rate."},"E383.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} checks Zib's calculations before returning the bills and discovers an error in the old statement. The banker pays for the correction in gold.","f":"{{heroName}} does not have time to reconcile all the accounts without beads. Zib demands that the tool be returned first."},"E383.4":{"s":"You leave the goblin bank without accounts. Behind his back, the boy happily moves the beads of the future financial crisis."},"E384.1":{"s":"You change the angle of the bucket and the package drops straight to the waiting recipient. Fluke pays in gold for the first delivery without bruises.","f":"The catapult jerks during launch, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded.","v":{"nf":"The launch turns out to be dangerous, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. They don't dare send the parcel."}},"E384.2":{"s":"You buy supplies from Fluke's assistants, while on the other side they demand that the shipment of frying pans be prohibited."},"E384.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} measures the wind and reduces the throwing distance; the box lands exactly in the marked circle. Fluke pays in gold.","f":"The lever suddenly releases the bucket, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded.","v":{"nf":"The ladle fires prematurely, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. The test is cancelled."}},"E384.4":{"s":"You refuse to send anything by air and continue on your way. Fluke is already recording the frying pan claim as a successful delivery."},"E385.1":{"s":"You return the pointer to the old mill and declare the path accessible to everyone. The angel and demon pay gold to end the dispute.","f":"Eriel and Hass each turn the sign in their own direction again. The neutral position could not be maintained."},"E385.2":{"s":"You pay for information about a safe route and leave, leaving Eriel and Hass to fight for the arrow."},"E385.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} suggests placing the temple and the fair on different sides of the sign. For completed proceedings you are given gold.","f":"The demon considers the decision a betrayal, and his assistants close the intersection. A skirmish begins."},"E385.4":{"s":"You choose the path yourself, without requiring the signature of heaven or hell. The old word \"mill\" disappears around the bend."},"E386.1":{"s":"You support Brak's scaffolding as he connects the two ends of the radiance without iron rivets. The dwarf thanks with gold.","f":"The scaffolding shifts under the masters, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded.","v":{"nf":"The scaffolding falls, but none of the available fighters are gravely wounded. The rainbow remains torn."}},"E386.2":{"s":"You give Lumi the supplies for the magical ritual, and she returns the flowers to their previous order. The fairy thanks with gold."},"E386.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} finds a way to secure the supports outside the glowing arc. Marriage pays gold for the rainbow saved.","f":"The metal clamp suddenly breaks free of its support and seriously injures {{affectedHeroName}}.","v":{"nf":"The staple disrupts the work, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. The gap remains the same."}},"E386.4":{"s":"You leave Brak to measure the rainbow with a ruler, and Lumi to be indignant at the word “staple.” The colors still don't match."},"E387.1":{"s":"You ask the young elves to wipe their boots before entering and acknowledge Drag's work. Elvy thanks the supplies for the tranquility of the garden.","f":"The students refuse to accept the order of their former enemy and continue to stand in front of the gate. The dispute is not resolved."},"E387.2":{"s":"Alvy sells you supplies from the garden warehouse. Drag meticulously checks the dirt on the boots of each porter."},"E387.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} convinces the young men to first watch how Drag takes care of the trees. Elvy thanks with gold for the peaceful passage.","f":"One of the students declares the conversation an insult to the fallen and calls his friends to a skirmish."},"E387.4":{"s":"You dry your feet and enter the garden without protesting to Drag. The orc nods approvingly, and the young elves turn away."},"E388.1":{"s":"You count skeletons by skulls, and Selius takes the number twenty-seven without fractions. Vessar pays in gold for the closed statement.","f":"A skeleton without a lower body requires double counting for independence. The argument goes back to the beginning."},"E388.2":{"s":"You buy supplies from Vessar while the angel continues to make calculations. One skeleton switches his leg to the other hand."},"E388.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} introduces a rule: each independent undead is counted once, regardless of the set of dice. The necromancer thanks with gold.","f":"Selius demands an additional column for missing limbs, and the statement again diverges."},"E388.4":{"s":"You leave the angel to count half the skeleton. He silently raises a separate leg as a sign of disagreement."},"E389.1":{"s":"You prove that one goblin also belongs to the “goblins” category, and Klep pays out the insurance. The dragon gives gold for mediation.","f":"Klep calls for armed assistants and demands to protect the agreement from dragon pressure. A skirmish begins."},"E389.2":{"s":"You pay part of the loss for Klep and end the argument before the air becomes fire. Iarax reluctantly cools down."},"E389.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} shows that the insured event is determined by theft, and not by the number of thieves. Klep gives out gold for an admitted mistake.","f":"{{heroName}} discovers a paid interpretation of the controversial point, and the treasury loses gold. Iarax continues to heat up."},"E389.4":{"s":"You move away from the insured fire while Klep argues about the number of goblins. The translator retreats after you."},"E390.1":{"s":"You follow the clear tracks and find the merchant in a hiding place along with his gold. Khar considers himself right up to the question of scratches.","f":"Human tracks lead to a prepared ambush. The battle begins."},"E390.2":{"s":"You pay Haru and Less for their different versions and continue on your way. Both insist that the other is wrong."},"E390.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} discovers that the scratches lead the armed pursuer away from the road, and the merchant actually walked himself. For the solution you get gold.","f":"At a branching trail, {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded by a hidden attacker.","v":{"nf":"The pursuer disrupts the reconnaissance, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. The traces remain undiscovered."}},"E390.4":{"s":"You don't become the third ranger. Khar and Less continue to argue over who owns the almost invisible scratch."},"E391.1":{"s":"You split Perra's hours between two weddings, and the proper music finally starts in both rooms. The musician pays in gold for the saved contract.","f":"The parties refuse to change the paid order of dances and demand Perra at the same time. It is not possible to reach an agreement."},"E391.2":{"s":"You buy supplies from the kitchen between two wedding feasts. From somewhere comes a melody in which the waltz argues with the march."},"E391.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} convinces families to exchange several guests and schedule performances. Perr thanks with gold.","f":"The orcs consider the transfer of the battle song an insult, and the people call their relatives for help. A skirmish begins."},"E391.4":{"s":"You leave before dancing together with axes. Perr remains between the halls with one lute and two schedules."},"E392.1":{"s":"You clear Lada's passage to P-12, and she carries out the necessary maintenance. The mechanic pays in gold for the saved machine gun.","f":"The pilgrims consider the tools an encroachment on the shrine and come out to defend P-12. A skirmish begins."},"E392.2":{"s":"You buy supplies from the pilgrims while P-12 reports another problem with the water pump."},"E392.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} explains to people that helping a child does not negate the need for repairs on the machine. The crowd lets Lada through, and she pays in gold.","f":"The pilgrims refuse to allow even a friendly mechanic to approach the machine. P-12 continues to require pump repair."},"E392.4":{"s":"You don't decide whether a repair machine can be considered holy. P-12 himself repeats the description of his previous work."},"E393.1":{"s":"You open a bridge that has been holding up builders for a week, and both craftsmen are entitled to their unit of length. The city pays in gold.","f":"Sael demands to write down the length in wind songs, but Durk is not ready to sign such an act. The opening has been delayed again."},"E393.2":{"s":"Builders sell you supplies while their authors argue about the number of feet in one wind song."},"E393.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} checks the fastenings and confirms that the bridge is safe regardless of the name of the units. Durk pays in gold.","f":"When tested, the support moves dangerously and seriously injures {{affectedHeroName}}.","v":{"nf":"The support fails the test, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. The bridge is temporarily closed."}},"E393.4":{"s":"You are crossing a bridge without dimensions. Sael and Durk don't even notice the new traveler in the midst of their argument."},"E394.1":{"s":"You take the letter from the skeleton and give it to Gass through the locked door. The demon thanks him with gold, without ever seeing the postman.","f":"Gass refuses to take the envelope even from living hands, fearing the touch of the undead. Delivery failed."},"E394.2":{"s":"You buy supplies from the innkeeper while Gass demands that the skeleton be kept away from his door."},"E394.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} explains to the demon that the letter does not turn into undead along with the postman. Gass opens the door and pays in gold.","f":"Gass mistakes the persuasion for an ambush and calls his armed acquaintances. A skirmish begins."},"E394.4":{"s":"You leave without trying to treat demonic fears. The skeleton calmly remains at the door with the unopened letter."},"E395.1":{"s":"You offer Tarr one bank, and the geese the other, leaving the water common. A fisherman shares supplies for a peaceful neighborhood.","f":"The geese disrupt the negotiations with a loud hiss, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded in the confusion.","v":{"nf":"Negotiations break down, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. The pond remains divided."}},"E395.2":{"s":"You buy supplies from the fisherman while the dragon on his shore is learning goose discipline."},"E395.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} finds Tarru another secluded place for the first treasures. The dragon gives golden thanks and leaves the geese.","f":"The irritated flock attacks the escorts, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded.","v":{"nf":"The pack drives off the escorts, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. Tarr remains by the pond."}},"E395.4":{"s":"You acknowledge the victory of the geese without a formal trial. Tarr angrily guards the three coins on his cramped shore."},"E396.1":{"s":"You call the yellow flower a garden plant that is forbidden to touch without the owner’s permission. S-9 accepts the rule, and Eli thanks him with supplies.","f":"The construct requires a botanical list of horticultural crops and does not accept verbal exceptions. Work remains stopped."},"E396.2":{"s":"You pay the gardener to cancel the order, and C-9 stops clearing the weeds. Eli stops covering the flower with his wings."},"E396.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} formulates a criterion that S-9 can check, and Eli recognizes as fair. The gardener thanks with gold.","f":"{{heroName}} does not find a definition without controversial exceptions. S-9 continues to wait for the work team."},"E396.4":{"s":"You leave the fairy and the construct to decide what a flower is. The gardener still hasn't returned from lunch."},"E397.1":{"s":"You help Horus light a fire and give Mera a comfortable rest. The angel thanks with supplies for your care, even if the halo is not shining yet.","f":"After the next decoction, the halo remains dark, and Horus admits that he has not found a way to repair it. There is no additional help."},"E397.2":{"s":"You leave supplies for the orc family, and Horus thanks you with gold. Mera holds the hot cup without any objection."},"E397.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} finds out together with Horus that the halo is hampered by a damaged mount, and not a cold. The shaman pays for repairs in gold.","f":"When tested, the halo discharges and seriously injures {{affectedHeroName}}.","v":{"nf":"The halo flares dangerously, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. The repair has to be postponed."}},"E397.4":{"s":"You leave the angel at the orc fire. Horus is still confident that warmth will one day help even the heavens."},"E398.1":{"s":"You finish watching the play without revealing the secret to the audience, and the village actors share supplies for their support. Feren finally remembers his last line.","f":"Feren forgets the whole ending when the real King rises from the bench. The show ends."},"E398.2":{"s":"You pay the troupe for a separate performance for the troop. Feren promises not to betray the real King, even by accident."},"E398.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} helps the director correct the most ridiculous facts, while maintaining a cheerful ending. The troupe thanks in gold.","f":"The director states that the exact story will ruin the dramatic effect. The rework is being postponed."},"E398.4":{"s":"You leave without revealing to the audience who was sitting among them. For a long time Feren portrays the royal bass more confidently than the original."},"E399.1":{"s":"You stop the skeleton horses and take Ian out of the last cart. Find suitable supplies among your luggage.","f":"The dead drivers return to their route and raise their weapons against those who stopped the caravan. The battle begins."},"E399.2":{"s":"You hand Ian the supplies and show him where it’s safe to get off at the turn. The boy remembers the directions until the carts slow down."},"E399.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} finds funeral words with which to complete the work of the drivers, and the caravan stops. Ian thanks with gold and supplies.","f":"The dead drivers respond to the ritual with a blow, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded.","v":{"nf":"The ritual is stopped due to the dangerous response of the undead, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. The caravan continues on its way."}},"E399.4":{"s":"You are moving away from carts that travel without living drivers. Ian remains in the last cart, looking at the road not to the house."},"E400.1":{"s":"You declare the road public and force the goblins to remove the booth. Delegations are given gold for open passage.","f":"All five parties consider the decision to be an infringement on their merits and are raising armed forces. The battle begins."},"E400.2":{"s":"You pay the goblins for passage and leave five delegations to argue over the sign. The booth immediately accepts the next client."},"E400.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} proposes to indicate on the stone the names of the builders, custodians and previous owners separately. The delegations are paid gold and supplies.","f":"One of the parties does not have enough space on the stone, the argument turns into a fight and a skirmish begins."},"E400.4":{"s":"You spend supplies on another route without waiting for the decision of the five delegations. Behind you, the goblins are already selling bypass cards."},"E401.1":{"s":"You keep the duelists from striking each other and point to the lagging bell. Both recognize the draw, and the townspeople pay in gold for the preserved peace.","f":"The nobles declare the intervention a violation of honor and draw their blades against the party. A skirmish begins."},"E401.2":{"s":"You pay Bran for repairs and pick up supplies to wait. In the square they are still arguing about what time the duel began."},"E401.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} discovers a secret delay in the striking mechanism and returns the ringing to the present hour. Bran thanks with gold and supplies.","f":"The heavy pendulum breaks during inspection and injures {{affectedHeroName}}.","v":{"nf":"The pendulum breaks off its support, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. They don't have time to fix the bell."}},"E401.4":{"s":"You are leaving a city where even the duelists were late for their own duel. The bell finally rings out yesterday's argument."},"E402.1":{"s":"You present the captain with the King's right to revoke an outdated order, and the main gates open for the first time in eighteen years. The townspeople return the illegally collected gold.","f":"The guards consider the attempt to cancel the order an outrage against the memory of the commandant and take up arms. A skirmish begins."},"E402.2":{"s":"You pay to pass through a narrow gate. Captain Nell carefully issues a receipt for the passage of one cart."},"E402.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} formalizes the legal cancellation of the siege order with a new date and seal. Nell thanks in gold for the opportunity to finally open the doors.","f":"{{heroName}} does not find the required signature in the old archives, and the guard collects a processing fee. The treasury is losing gold."},"E402.4":{"s":"You spend supplies on the outer circuit of the city. Outside the walls, residents continue to squeeze carts through the gate."},"E403.1":{"s":"You open the gates of the village, and people come out without obstacles. Grateful residents give the party supplies from Seven's reserves.","f":"The orderlies block the road with batons and call in armed quarantine guards. A skirmish begins."},"E403.2":{"s":"You buy medicines and provisions from the quarantine warehouse. Seven warmly congratulates the party for being symptom-free."},"E403.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} checks the histories of patients and discovers that the list of the dead is made up of living residents. The village pays gold for exposure.","f":"The sanitary protection is triggered when the closed ward is opened, seriously injuring {{affectedHeroName}}.","v":{"nf":"The chamber's defense stops the check, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. The quarantine has not been lifted."}},"E403.4":{"s":"You leave the city outside the gates, where everyone's health is declared to be the merit of the doctor. Seven is already congratulating the next traveler."},"E404.1":{"s":"Laurent agrees to pay for a temporary crossing while workers fix the overturned deck. The party is given gold for their assistance in the investigation.","f":"The contractor sticks to the literal drawing and refuses to admit the mistake. There is no temporary crossing."},"E404.2":{"s":"You pay the workers for temporary flooring and go through the ravine. Part of the supplies goes to strengthen the crossing."},"E404.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} finds a reliable bottom beam and strengthens the passage for people. For safe passage, the workers leave behind some supplies.","f":"The fastening is torn off from the lower deck, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded.","v":{"nf":"The deck swings dangerously, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. The test ends."}},"E404.4":{"s":"You spend your provisions on a long walk around a bridge where the top and bottom are mixed up. Laurent continues to refer to the drawing."},"E405.1":{"s":"You intercept the carriage before descending, and Remus finally calls the meeting adjourned. The judge thanks in gold for saving the process.","f":"The carriage jerks sharply as it turns, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded.","v":{"nf":"The cart is abandoned at a turn, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. It is impossible to stop her."}},"E405.2":{"s":"You place a cart loaded with supplies across the path, and the carriage stops. Rem pays for the damage in gold.","f":"The carriage breaks through the barrier and carries away part of the provisions under the wheels. The judge continues the hearing on the move."},"E405.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} catches up with the horses and takes the reins to the stone slope. Rem pays gold for helping the court.","f":"On the side of the road, the horse jumps sharply, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded.","v":{"nf":"The horses foil the interception attempt, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. The carriage goes down the road."}},"E405.4":{"s":"You step out of the way, allowing the court to move on its own. Following this comes Koster’s new confession about a crime that did not happen."},"E406.1":{"s":"You explain to the officer that Krum teaches recruits to survive defeat, not strive for it. The veteran thanks the supplies for the support.","f":"The officer demands to stop the classes as disgraceful, but Krum is not ready to give in. The dispute continues."},"E406.2":{"s":"Krum agrees to teach your party not only to fight, but also to lay down their weapons in time. He goes on a campaign.","f":"The veteran decides that the students in the meadow need his experience more, and refuses the invitation.","v":{"rs":"Krum agrees to serve, but there is no free space for a new fighter. He hands over some gold in gratitude for the respect."}},"E406.3":{"s":"Recruits line up for a training skirmish and demonstrate how quickly they can admit defeat. Krum happily commands to begin the check."},"E406.4":{"s":"You leave Krum to teach useful military skills. The young officer is trying to understand whether it is possible to give the command “surrender” in a combatant voice."},"E407.1":{"s":"The children admit to the apple tree that its fruits were good in themselves. Apples appear on the branches again, and the gardener gives out supplies.","f":"The children say an apology too rote, and the branches defiantly turn away. There is no harvest yet."},"E407.2":{"s":"You buy last year's supplies from gardeners. Ciel reminds everyone not to compare their taste to pears."},"E407.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} conducts a ceremony of gratitude for the previous harvest, and the apple tree stops shedding ovaries. The party is preparing supplies.","f":"The incorrect rhythm of the ritual causes the branches to drop more of the collected supplies. Ciel asks to stop trying."},"E407.4":{"s":"You leave the children to ask forgiveness from the apple tree, which covered its ears with its branches. Ciel is preparing a new speech."},"E408.1":{"s":"You sing the memorized part of the melody and find a cache of supplies near the real pass. Liar nods approvingly.","f":"An incomplete song again leads to a ravine, and even more supplies are spent searching for the road."},"E408.2":{"s":"You pay the hunter for a journey that does not require singing. He shows a quiet path around a familiar ravine."},"E408.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} picks up the end of the melody according to the pattern of the fabric, and the map shows the whole path for the first time. The party finds supplies.","f":"One wrong note leads to a dead end, and part of the provisions is spent on the return."},"E408.4":{"s":"You take the ordinary path, spending supplies on the longer journey. Orin continues humming half the map."},"E409.1":{"s":"You stop the deer and return the letter to Neri before Talen appears. The archer thanks in gold for the opportunity to say everything herself.","f":"The deer sneaks away to the temple road and does not allow the message to be taken away. Neri will have to meet her husband after the delivery."},"E409.2":{"s":"You allow the deer to hand the letter to Talen. He reads it in front of Neri, and the spouses have nowhere else to hide the conversation."},"E409.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} comes across the messenger and gently removes the letter from the green ribbon. Neri thanks with gold.","f":"The deer sharply fights back with its antlers, and {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded.","v":{"nf":"The envoy drives off the interceptors, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. The letter remains with the deer."}},"E409.4":{"s":"You leave, leaving Neri to decide how to speak to Talen. The deer is already moving towards the familiar voice."},"E410.1":{"s":"You help Elven clear the basins from the spring, and the silver water flows freely again. The keeper thanks with supplies.","f":"The washers refer to the literal text of the ban and do not release the water. The queue of baskets is growing."},"E410.2":{"s":"You pay for water and replenish your camping supplies. Elven watches the basins with the air of a man who has lost a thousand years of tradition."},"E410.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} offers a separate stream for washing and a ritual of cleansing the source itself. The elves agree and share the supplies.","f":"Water leaves the old riverbed during work, and some of the supplies spoil. Elven demands that everything be returned to the way it was."},"E410.4":{"s":"You leave the elves to argue about thousand-year-old traditions and dirty shirts. The queue to the source is not getting shorter."},"E411.1":{"s":"Wissa hits the bell behind the screen and wins the tournament. You take gold at a successful bet.","f":"Vissa's arrow goes past the ringing, and your bet remains with the manager. The merchant with the broken hat is not happy."},"E411.2":{"s":"You take the spectators beyond the safe line, and the judge is forced to recognize the wind as not the only danger. For helping the party, they are given supplies.","f":"Airen considers the transfer of the public a violation of ancient rules, and the shooters continue to prepare at the same screen."},"E411.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} finds in the rules the judge’s right to expand the protective circle and forces him to fulfill it. Airen pays in gold for saving the tournament.","f":"{{heroName}} does not have time to convince the judges before the next shot, and the organizers charge a fee for verification. The treasury is losing gold."},"E411.4":{"s":"You leave the tournament until you reach a new random target. The merchant carefully folds his holey hat."},"E412.1":{"s":"You find a clue in the tracks: the last figure allowed the dancers to disperse and meet again. Aerin thanks the supplies for the restoration.","f":"The old prints move in different directions, leaving not a single reliable step. The ritual continues endlessly."},"E412.2":{"s":"Aerin agrees to honestly call the new movement new and allows the dance to finish. The elves give thanks with gold for the saved future.","f":"The elders do not want to introduce innovation into a hundred-year-old ritual. The forty-eighth step remains empty."},"E412.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} finds the meaning of the last figure in old songs and restores the ritual. Aerin hands over the gold.","f":"When trying to repeat the lost figure, the security sign is triggered, seriously injuring {{affectedHeroName}}.","v":{"nf":"A security sign interrupts the dance, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. The last step has not yet been restored."}},"E412.4":{"s":"You leave the elves the right to come up with or restore the ending of the dance. Aerin is still studying the old tracks."},"E413.1":{"s":"Both clans try two stews and agree that neither is worse than the other. The groom gives the party supplies after the dispute is over.","f":"Shaman Targa declares the tasting a violation of the ritual, and armed supporters converge at the cauldron. A skirmish begins."},"E413.2":{"s":"You buy several pots of sacred stew from Groom and replenish your supplies. Targa insists not to call her dinner."},"E413.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} combines two recipes so that each clan recognizes the taste of their ancestors. The party receives supplies from satisfied cooks.","f":"The elders notice the deception and accuse those who mixed the recipes of sacrilege. A skirmish begins."},"E413.4":{"s":"You leave while the orcs share the authorship of the stew. Targa is already asking for a fourth bowl purely for testing purposes."},"E414.1":{"s":"You remind the council that Mogra raised Ian for five years, and the stone does not know the family. The clan recognizes the boy as one of their own and gives him supplies.","f":"Burg insists on the old test, not allowing it to be replaced by family recognition. The decision is postponed."},"E414.2":{"s":"Yang is tested on his knowledge of the language and history of the clan, and the elder recognizes this as a real test. Mogra thanks with gold.","f":"Some of the soldiers consider the new test a mockery and come out to defend the old order by force. A skirmish begins."},"E414.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} comes up with a long journey with heavy but feasible equipment, and Ian endures it. Burg thanks in gold for the honest replacement.","f":"During the test, a support breaks off and seriously injures {{affectedHeroName}}.","v":{"nf":"The test has to be aborted due to a dangerous breakdown, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. Ian remains to wait for a decision."}},"E414.4":{"s":"You leave Mogra and Yan in front of the elder with the ritual stone. The boy tightens his grip on the handle of someone else's large axe."},"E415.1":{"s":"You propose to count only wounds received in battle and confirmed by witnesses. Ugrat gives out gold for an understandable statement.","f":"Krosh finds new witnesses to his cut hand and demands that it be considered a combat hand. The line is arguing again."},"E415.2":{"s":"Krosh convinces the paymaster to consider the cut an army injury, and your bet brings in gold.","f":"Ugrat recognizes the cut as domestic, and the placed bet remains with the bookmakers."},"E415.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} examines the scars and confirmations separately, closing the dispute about a long wound and two short ones. The treasurer pays in gold.","f":"{{heroName}} does not find the necessary records, and the treasury loses gold during the investigation. Ugrat returns to his calculations."},"E415.4":{"s":"You don’t undertake to determine the price of other people’s scars. Krosh is ready to demonstrate how he received a cut at the treasury."},"E416.1":{"s":"You detain the scout without the participation of Shmyg, and Gark gives gold for help. The boar continues to study the flowers.","f":"The scout calls his guards, and the interception turns into a skirmish."},"E416.2":{"s":"You buy camp food from Gark, which Shmyg no longer wants to eat before the battle. The orc sighs over the remaining bag."},"E416.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} calmly takes Shmyg out of the way without demanding an attack. Gark thanks in gold for the returned boar.","f":"The boar is frightened by an attempt to move it and gravely wounds {{affectedHeroName}}.","v":{"nf":"Shmyg pushes away the escorts, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. The boar remains near the flowers."}},"E416.4":{"s":"You respect Shmyg’s decision not to fight today. Gark once again asks the boar to at least look menacingly."},"E417.1":{"s":"The ambassador accepts the idea of peace with three clans at once, and Rag finally stops waiting for a new war. The party is paid in gold for saving diplomacy.","f":"Hara considers the new interpretation a provocation and brings supporters into conflict."},"E417.2":{"s":"You pay the tattoo artist for the correction and Rag receives a contract with the correct name on the back. The master gives out supplies for help."},"E417.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} finds in the old rite the right to inscribe the name of the third clan as a sign of a future truce. Khara thanks with gold.","f":"{{heroName}} cannot find a recognized interpretation for the erroneous inscription. Hara continues to demand correction."},"E417.4":{"s":"You leave Raga before the third clan arrives. The leader finally asks for a mirror to see his own back."},"E418.1":{"s":"You use up supplies to bypass the nearby river. Kuga continues to remember what crossing the drum asked about."},"E418.2":{"s":"You cross the nearby river without incident and find some remaining supplies on the far bank.","f":"At the crossing, {{affectedHeroName}} is gravely wounded due to a sudden rise in water.","v":{"nf":"The water rises dangerously, but none of the eligible fighters is gravely wounded. The crossing must be abandoned."}},"E418.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} restores yesterday's order of beats and understands that the drum warned about a distant river. Kuga gives out supplies for finding the answer.","f":"To repeat the ritual, supplies are consumed, but the drum remains silent until the next day. Checking doesn't help."},"E418.4":{"s":"You leave without checking the prophecy with a daily delay. Kuga is already preparing a new question that he will forget tomorrow."},"E419.1":{"s":"You separate the voices from the silence, and the inhabitants of the necropolis choose the headman by real counting. The commission thanks in gold.","f":"Some voters are unable to leave their graves, and candidates are debating how to account for absences. The results have not been confirmed."},"E419.2":{"s":"You support the commission with gold, and it gives out supplies for the journey in gratitude. Additional urns are finally being taken out of the ground."},"E419.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} finds a rule in the charter: those who do not vote are not considered a supporter of the current government. The necropolis pays in gold for a clear outcome.","f":"{{heroName}} does not find an article about voting by those who do not physically stand up, and the dispute requires a paid hearing. The treasury is losing gold."},"E419.4":{"s":"You leave the necropolis to decide whose silence is the voice. Hess is already ordering a new lantern for the polling station."},"E420.1":{"s":"You show Bem the location of the old house on Cora's map, and the ghost stops tormenting the new owner. The grateful widow gives out supplies.","f":"Bem refuses to believe that the real house has been demolished and again demands a confession from the current occupant. The problem is not resolved."},"E420.2":{"s":"You buy old supplies from the cellar from Cora while Bem studies a map of the city's lots."},"E420.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} takes Bem to his former home and ends the conversation with the past without new accusations. The widow thanks in gold.","f":"A hostile seal appears on the old site and seriously injures {{affectedHeroName}}.","v":{"nf":"The old seal interferes with the ritual, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. Bem continues to look for the culprit."}},"E420.4":{"s":"You leave, leaving Bem to argue with the city number plate. The current owner of the house finally locks the door at night."},"E421.1":{"s":"In the depths of the cellar, a secret door to an old tunnel is discovered and a gold payment left by the thieves is discovered. Laurent asks for the first time who knew about the passage.","f":"Armed servants of an unknown buyer emerge from the tunnel. A skirmish begins."},"E421.2":{"s":"You sell supplies to Laurent, and the vampire pays in gold, without explaining why the empty cellar needs them."},"E421.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} notices that the manager’s entries were made not by hand, but by a mechanism that repeats it. Laurent thanks the gold for the solution.","f":"{{heroName}} cannot prove the records were falsified, and the manager charges an audit fee. The treasury is losing gold."},"E421.4":{"s":"You leave Laurent among the empty shelves and don’t ask what exactly was in the bottles. The skeleton recalculates zero again."},"E422.1":{"s":"You open the chest that Arkat checked outside three times and find his priceless item next to the gold. The lich closes the lid with relief.","f":"The chest responds with a defensive flash, and {{affectedHeroName}} is severely wounded.","v":{"nf":"The chest's protection is triggered, but no eligible fighters are gravely wounded. Arkat continues his search."}},"E422.2":{"s":"You leave supplies for Arkat to continue his search, and the lich pays in gold. The skeletons are already rearranging the furniture for the fourth time."},"E422.3":{"s":"One of the skeletons, relieved, agrees to serve the King instead of searching for the lost item. He joins the party.","f":"The skeleton is afraid that Arkat will notice his absence before he disappears, and remains in the laboratory.","v":{"rs":"The skeleton agrees to leave the laboratory, but there is no place in the party. He thanks the gold and returns to his search."}},"E422.4":{"s":"You don’t ask why the lich is so inconvenient to exist without. Behind him, the skeleton again points to the chest lid."},"E423.1":{"s":"You bring the living Fel out from under the burial cloth, and he shares the supplies he found. Mor threatens to file a shortage report.","f":"Pestilence calls in armed gravediggers, considering the rescue a violation of the paid transportation. A skirmish begins."},"E423.2":{"s":"You pay for the correction of the statement, Fel gets out of the wagon and gives you travel supplies in gratitude."},"E423.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} removes the canvas while Mort counts the bodies, and Fel slides onto the road. The rescued person donates supplies.","f":"The driver notices the disappearance of the passenger and calls for an armed funeral team. A skirmish begins."},"E423.4":{"s":"You do not argue with the cemetery service, where the living were recorded as dead. Fel continues to wave from under the canvas."},"E424.1":{"s":"You find old children's things and a closed golden casket in the crypt. The song fades out on the last line.","f":"The words of the lullaby awaken the armed inhabitants of the crypt. The battle begins."},"E424.2":{"s":"You leave supplies for the gravediggers to strengthen the entrance, and Vienna thanks you with gold. The request still sounds from underground."},"E424.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} conducts a ritual of remembrance at the old crypt, and the voices calm down. Vienna gives out gold and supplies for restored peace.","f":"The funeral seal retaliates and gravely wounds {{affectedHeroName}}.","v":{"nf":"The seal breaks the ritual, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. The lullaby continues."}},"E424.4":{"s":"You leave the cemetery before nightfall. The last line of the lullaby can even be heard on the road."},"E425.1":{"s":"The spider finally approaches Daren, and he receives the scroll in front of witnesses. Veira pays in gold to finish the long delivery.","f":"Daren calls armed friends against the attempt to force him to accept the letter. A skirmish begins."},"E425.2":{"s":"Veera and Daren agree to speak to each other without an eight-legged intermediary. For ending the dispute, you are given gold.","f":"Both insist on observing the wedding rites, and the spider continues to sit between them. The conversation doesn't work out."},"E425.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} calms the spider and brings it to Daren with a scroll on his paw. Veira thanks with gold.","f":"The spider turns sharply on its leash and seriously injures {{affectedHeroName}}.","v":{"nf":"The spider refuses to go and pushes away those accompanying him, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. The letter was not delivered."}},"E425.4":{"s":"You leave spouses arguing about a divorce that requires a spider. He makes himself comfortable next to Daren."},"E426.1":{"s":"You convince clients to pay for materials, travel, and contract contingencies. The Guild thanks in gold for ending the strike.","f":"One of the customers declares the negotiators to be accomplices of the strikers and grabs his weapon. A skirmish begins."},"E426.2":{"s":"You pay for passage through the guild territory. Assassins with empty scabbards politely let the party through."},"E426.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} separates the fixed fee and the costs of fulfilling orders; both sides accept the new table. The guild pays in gold.","f":"{{heroName}} does not convince clients to accept surcharges, and the guild collects a mediation fee. The treasury is losing gold."},"E426.4":{"s":"You spend supplies going around the block of striking killers. Saris continues to assure passersby that they are safe today."},"E427.1":{"s":"You stop dissatisfied customers, and Illis removes the mirror from the street. The merchant thanks the gold for saving the shop.","f":"The customers decide to break the mirror along with the security, and a confrontation ensues at the counter."},"E427.2":{"s":"You buy supplies from Illis instead of an obsidian mirror. It manages to inform the merchant that the price tag is really too high."},"E427.3":{"s":"Illis returns the buyers' money and pays the party gold to settle the claims.","f":"Illis announces that the truth cannot be returned as a defective product. Buyers are left without money."},"E427.4":{"s":"You leave without asking the mirror what it thinks of the King. It suddenly notices loudly that silence also says a lot."},"E428.1":{"s":"Liassa chooses where and with whom she wants to live, and both matrons are forced to hear her answer. The girl thanks the supplies for the right to speak.","f":"Liassa is not ready to decide in front of two arguing mothers and asks to be left alone. The dispute is still ongoing."},"E428.2":{"s":"You do not interfere in a generic dispute between two genuine contracts. Liassa stares after her without saying a word."},"E428.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} finds a separate contract for the exchange of children, signed by both matrons that very night. Families pay in gold for the truth restored.","f":"{{heroName}} is faced with two legitimate but conflicting receipts; the parties demand payment for the proceedings. The treasury is losing gold."},"E428.4":{"s":"Liassa agrees to go with the King to make decisions outside of the two houses for the first time. She joins the party.","f":"The matrons call the guards and forbid Liassa to leave with strangers. A skirmish begins.","v":{"rs":"Liassa is ready to go on a hike, but there is no place in the party. In gratitude for the proposed way out, she hands over the gold."}},"E429.1":{"s":"You discover the hitman before the strike and force him to renege on his contract. Iara pays in gold for her life saved.","f":"The perpetrator reveals the ambush only after dark and brings armed accomplices. The battle begins."},"E429.2":{"s":"You pay the cancellation fee and Kes receives written confirmation from the guild. The grateful student returns the gold to the party.","f":"The contractor has already started the task and refuses to cancel it even for a fee. Negotiations do not save a mentor."},"E429.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} notices a man among passers-by who never takes his eyes off Iara. For a revealed observer, the student pays in gold.","f":"The Observer injures {{affectedHeroName}} before he can be removed from the crowd.","v":{"nf":"The Observer escapes after a dangerous skirmish, but none of the eligible fighters are gravely wounded. The performer remains unknown."}},"E429.4":{"s":"You refuse to participate in the final exam to kill your own teacher. Kes again begs Iara to hide."},"E430.1":{"s":"You repeat the gesture of an experienced buyer and quietly exit the auction with a golden profit. Sel bows his head politely.","f":"Sel accepts the motion to raise the rate and exacts a fine in gold for breaking the rules. The party has to pay."},"E430.2":{"s":"You pay the penalty for the wrong bet and leave the silent hall. The auctioneer doesn't even raise her voice."},"E430.3":{"s":"{{heroName}} quickly masters sign language and resells the bet to another guest. The treasury receives gold.","f":"{{heroName}} confuses the refusal sign with an additional bet, and the party loses gold."},"E430.4":{"s":"The king loudly says “no” and immediately leaves the hall according to the rule about violators. Sel points to the exit without a word."}});
